WEBVTT

1
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.375
In verse 13.23,

2
00:00:31.375 --> 00:00:34.250
Lord Krishna mentions the Paramatma.

3
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:38.125
He says the Paramatma is distinct
from the jivatma.

4
00:00:38.125 --> 00:00:41.291
The Paramatma is the other purusha
within this body.

5
00:00:41.291 --> 00:00:43.000
Both the Paramatma and the jivatma

6
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.083
dwell within the body, but

7
00:00:46.083 --> 00:00:48.791
their roles are different.

8
00:00:48.791 --> 00:00:52.000
The jivatma, driven by desires,

9
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.250
seeks to enjoy the material world

10
00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:57.500
and becomes entangled in the
cycle of birth and death.

11
00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:00.625
The Paramatma, by contrast, is divine.

12
00:01:00.625 --> 00:01:02.375
He functions as the permission-giver,

13
00:01:02.375 --> 00:01:05.708
the supreme controller, and the witness.

14
00:01:10.375 --> 00:01:14.416
Lord Krishna says, ‘upadrashtanumanta ca’.

15
00:01:14.416 --> 00:01:17.166
This means the Paramatma functions
as the upadrashtā,

16
00:01:17.166 --> 00:01:19.583
and as the anumanta.

17
00:01:19.583 --> 00:01:21.166
Upadrashtā -

18
00:01:21.166 --> 00:01:24.333
the witness who sees all.

19
00:01:24.333 --> 00:01:26.208
Anumanta -

20
00:01:26.208 --> 00:01:29.416
The one who gives the jivatma permission

21
00:01:29.416 --> 00:01:32.416
to act according to its desires.

22
00:01:32.416 --> 00:01:33.875
The Paramatma observes

23
00:01:33.875 --> 00:01:35.708
the jivatma's actions

24
00:01:35.708 --> 00:01:37.416
and permits its desires

25
00:01:37.416 --> 00:01:38.375
to be fulfilled

26
00:01:38.375 --> 00:01:41.125
in accordance with it’s past karma.

27
00:01:41.125 --> 00:01:43.958
Without the Paramatma's sanction, the jivatma

28
00:01:43.958 --> 00:01:46.125
cannot perform any action.

29
00:01:46.125 --> 00:01:49.916
The Paramatma is also bharta bhokta Maheshvarah,

30
00:01:49.916 --> 00:01:51.541
meaning he is -

31
00:01:51.541 --> 00:01:53.708
the sustainer, the supreme enjoyer,

32
00:01:53.708 --> 00:01:55.833
and the highest controller.

33
00:01:55.833 --> 00:01:57.208
Bharta means

34
00:01:57.208 --> 00:02:00.833
the Paramatma nourishes all living beings

35
00:02:00.833 --> 00:02:02.583
and provides what is needed

36
00:02:02.583 --> 00:02:04.125
for their desires

37
00:02:04.125 --> 00:02:06.625
to be fulfilled.

38
00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:09.250
Bhokta means that although the jivatma

39
00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:12.291
tries to enjoy material pleasures,

40
00:02:12.291 --> 00:02:15.375
the ultimate enjoyer of all activities

41
00:02:15.375 --> 00:02:17.208
is the Paramatma.

42
00:02:17.208 --> 00:02:20.208
Maheshvara means the Supreme Lord,

43
00:02:20.208 --> 00:02:22.375
the highest master

44
00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:24.000
and controller of all.

45
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.791
Lord Krishna clarifies

46
00:02:25.791 --> 00:02:28.583
that the Paramatma is purushah parah,

47
00:02:28.583 --> 00:02:31.375
the transcendental purusha, who
remains beyond

48
00:02:31.375 --> 00:02:32.583
material nature

49
00:02:32.583 --> 00:02:35.291
and is unaffected by its qualities.

50
00:02:35.291 --> 00:02:38.166
Though He dwells within the body,

51
00:02:38.166 --> 00:02:39.291
He is not bound

52
00:02:39.291 --> 00:02:41.666
by the material conditions

53
00:02:41.666 --> 00:02:44.166
that bind the jivatma.

54
00:02:44.166 --> 00:02:47.583
The jivatma experiences joy and sorrow

55
00:02:47.583 --> 00:02:49.625
because of its identification with the body.

56
00:02:49.625 --> 00:02:52.333
But the Paramatma remains neutral.

57
00:02:52.333 --> 00:02:55.041
He observes the jivatma's actions

58
00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:56.625
and gives permission,

59
00:02:56.625 --> 00:02:58.791
but does not Himself become entangled.

60
00:02:58.791 --> 00:03:01.458
A well-known example

61
00:03:01.458 --> 00:03:03.500
explains this relationship:

62
00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:06.083
two birds are sitting on the same tree.

63
00:03:06.083 --> 00:03:08.583
The jivatma is like the bird

64
00:03:08.583 --> 00:03:10.541
that tastes the fruits of the tree,

65
00:03:10.541 --> 00:03:13.000
experiencing joy and sorrow.

66
00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.708
The Paramatma is like the second bird

67
00:03:15.708 --> 00:03:17.250
who only watches,

68
00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:20.000
unaffected by the fruits.

69
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.250
The jivatma, through ignorance, keeps enjoying

70
00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:25.166
or suffering.

71
00:03:25.166 --> 00:03:26.375
While the Paramatma

72
00:03:26.375 --> 00:03:29.541
waits patiently for the soul

73
00:03:29.541 --> 00:03:33.416
to turn toward Him for guidance and liberation.

74
00:03:33.416 --> 00:03:37.000
In the Gita, the Paramatma is
described in other places too.

75
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:40.250
All these references confirm

76
00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:41.083
that the Paramatma,

77
00:03:41.083 --> 00:03:42.458
even while dwelling within

78
00:03:42.458 --> 00:03:44.125
all beings,

79
00:03:44.125 --> 00:03:47.166
remains beyond the limitations
of the material world

80
00:03:47.166 --> 00:03:49.958
and is the supreme source of guidance

81
00:03:49.958 --> 00:03:51.166
and sanction.

82
00:03:55.916 --> 00:03:59.125
Have you ever said,

83
00:03:59.125 --> 00:04:03.250
'Why did God do this to me?'

84
00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:05.458
Especially

85
00:04:05.458 --> 00:04:07.875
when something goes wrong,

86
00:04:07.875 --> 00:04:10.833
when plans fall apart, people

87
00:04:10.833 --> 00:04:12.541
hurt you,

88
00:04:12.541 --> 00:04:15.250
or life seems unfair?

89
00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:17.625
Let Me tell you this,

90
00:04:17.625 --> 00:04:21.000
as the Paramatma,

91
00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.791
I do not do anything to you.

92
00:04:23.791 --> 00:04:26.875
I only watch

93
00:04:26.875 --> 00:04:30.125
and give permission.

94
00:04:30.125 --> 00:04:34.958
You make the choices, you hold the desires,

95
00:04:34.958 --> 00:04:36.333
and as a loving witness

96
00:04:36.333 --> 00:04:39.708
in your heart,

97
00:04:39.708 --> 00:04:43.041
I give you the freedom

98
00:04:43.041 --> 00:04:45.000
to follow them.

99
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.541
This does not mean

100
00:04:47.541 --> 00:04:49.833
I want you

101
00:04:49.833 --> 00:04:53.291
to take a particular path.

102
00:04:53.291 --> 00:04:55.333
It only means

103
00:04:55.333 --> 00:05:01.208
I have respected your free will.

104
00:05:01.208 --> 00:05:04.916
I let you make your journey,

105
00:05:04.916 --> 00:05:07.750
and I walk with you,

106
00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:10.208
because I know that

107
00:05:10.208 --> 00:05:13.583
you may lose your way.

108
00:05:13.583 --> 00:05:17.250
When your desires bring you sorrow,

109
00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:21.000
I do not leave you.

110
00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:24.833
I remain quietly present,

111
00:05:24.833 --> 00:05:30.625
ready to guide you back,

112
00:05:30.625 --> 00:05:33.000
If you will look toward Me,

113
00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:36.750
I never compel you,

114
00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:40.541
but I never abandon you either.

115
00:05:40.541 --> 00:05:43.000
So the next time

116
00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:48.000
you feel disappointed or lost,

117
00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.083
do not ask,

118
00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:53.000
'Why did God do this?'

119
00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.333
Ask instead,

120
00:05:55.333 --> 00:05:59.000
'What can I learn from this?'

121
00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:03.000
Because I am still here,

122
00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.208
in your heart,

123
00:06:06.208 --> 00:06:09.458
patiently waiting,

124
00:06:09.458 --> 00:06:13.750
lovingly watching, and quietly

125
00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:17.541
whispering the way back.

126
00:06:22.333 --> 00:06:24.041
When people see

127
00:06:24.041 --> 00:06:28.500
injustice, violence, or suffering in society,

128
00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:30.291
they often say,

129
00:06:30.291 --> 00:06:33.500
'If God exists, why is the world like this?'

130
00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:34.875
Let Me clarify something

131
00:06:34.875 --> 00:06:38.416
for this question,

132
00:06:38.416 --> 00:06:41.666
I am not the cause of these problems.

133
00:06:41.666 --> 00:06:45.000
As the Paramatma, I only watch

134
00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.791
and give permission,

135
00:06:47.791 --> 00:06:49.291
I do not force

136
00:06:49.291 --> 00:06:52.250
anyone to act.

137
00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:56.708
Every person has been given free will.

138
00:06:56.708 --> 00:07:00.708
And what we see around us

139
00:07:00.708 --> 00:07:04.166
is the result of how that freedom

140
00:07:04.166 --> 00:07:08.458
is used or misused.

141
00:07:08.458 --> 00:07:10.041
It is like a person

142
00:07:10.041 --> 00:07:13.416
who refuses to visit the barber

143
00:07:13.416 --> 00:07:16.458
and then blames the barber

144
00:07:16.458 --> 00:07:20.250
for their tangled hair.

145
00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:21.583
The problem is not

146
00:07:21.583 --> 00:07:24.750
the absence of help, the problem is

147
00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:26.916
refusing to receive it.

148
00:07:26.916 --> 00:07:29.541
In family or society, when people

149
00:07:29.541 --> 00:07:31.166
stop listening to the voice

150
00:07:31.166 --> 00:07:32.625
of their conscience,

151
00:07:32.625 --> 00:07:36.041
where I dwell,

152
00:07:36.041 --> 00:07:37.458
when they disconnect from values

153
00:07:37.458 --> 00:07:41.000
and spiritual guidance,

154
00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:43.083
things naturally begin

155
00:07:43.083 --> 00:07:44.541
to go wrong.

156
00:07:44.541 --> 00:07:47.458
But even then I do not leave.

157
00:07:47.458 --> 00:07:50.541
I remain in every heart,

158
00:07:50.541 --> 00:07:52.833
always ready to guide

159
00:07:52.833 --> 00:07:55.750
again and again,

160
00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:58.666
if they are willing to listen.

161
00:07:58.666 --> 00:08:02.333
So instead of placing blame on Me,

162
00:08:02.333 --> 00:08:04.958
become an instrument of change.

163
00:08:04.958 --> 00:08:06.583
Teach your children the importance

164
00:08:06.583 --> 00:08:09.625
of making right choices.

165
00:08:09.625 --> 00:08:12.541
Inspire your family to live

166
00:08:12.541 --> 00:08:15.375
with responsibility.

167
00:08:15.375 --> 00:08:20.416
This is how we begin to bring change to society.

168
00:08:25.125 --> 00:08:28.625
As you progress in leadership,

169
00:08:28.625 --> 00:08:31.000
your role changes.

170
00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:33.958
You are no longer only the one doing the work,

171
00:08:33.958 --> 00:08:35.833
you become the one

172
00:08:35.833 --> 00:08:38.541
overseeing and guiding.

173
00:08:38.541 --> 00:08:40.166
In this verse

174
00:08:40.166 --> 00:08:45.000
I describe Myself as the upadrashtā,

175
00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.875
the observer,

176
00:08:46.875 --> 00:08:51.708
and the anumanta, the permission-giver.

177
00:08:51.708 --> 00:08:54.000
I do not interfere,

178
00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:57.833
but I watch. I do not compel,

179
00:08:57.833 --> 00:09:02.291
but I permit. And in doing so,

180
00:09:02.291 --> 00:09:06.000
I help others grow.

181
00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:09.750
Effective leadership looks exactly like this.

182
00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:11.250
It is not about

183
00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:14.416
controlling every detail.

184
00:09:14.416 --> 00:09:16.458
It is about observing carefully,

185
00:09:16.458 --> 00:09:19.000
stepping in when needed,

186
00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:21.166
and inspiring your team

187
00:09:21.166 --> 00:09:24.583
to take ownership.

188
00:09:24.583 --> 00:09:26.750
When you guide

189
00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:29.125
without control,

190
00:09:29.125 --> 00:09:32.458
your people do not merely perform,

191
00:09:32.458 --> 00:09:34.625
they also develop.

192
00:09:34.625 --> 00:09:37.208
Being a permission-giver means

193
00:09:37.208 --> 00:09:39.291
This means -

194
00:09:39.291 --> 00:09:41.791
granting thoughtful permission,

195
00:09:41.791 --> 00:09:44.083
not blind approval.

196
00:09:44.083 --> 00:09:47.125
It means encouraging others
to take responsibility,

197
00:09:47.125 --> 00:09:48.291
make decisions,

198
00:09:48.291 --> 00:09:53.333
and learn from their outcomes.

199
00:09:53.333 --> 00:09:58.125
You remain available as a steady guide,

200
00:09:58.125 --> 00:10:02.708
not as a hovering supervisor.

201
00:10:02.708 --> 00:10:05.416
When you lead this way,

202
00:10:05.416 --> 00:10:08.416
you become far more than a senior

203
00:10:08.416 --> 00:10:10.833
official,

204
00:10:10.833 --> 00:10:14.208
you become a bharta,

205
00:10:14.208 --> 00:10:17.250
a true nourisher of abilities.

206
00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:20.541
And like the Paramatma present in every heart,

207
00:10:20.541 --> 00:10:21.708
you will be respected

208
00:10:21.708 --> 00:10:23.333
not for

209
00:10:23.333 --> 00:10:25.500
how vocal you are,

210
00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:27.666
but for the quality

211
00:10:27.666 --> 00:10:30.833
of your presence,

212
00:10:30.833 --> 00:10:35.750
calm, clear, and quietly empowering.

213
00:10:35.750 --> 00:10:38.166
This is the finest leadership.
